 "limits": [
  "an ancestor site is a bounded pattern whose named prefix is non-empty and shorter than the face's own directory list; a depth-0 site (``*/**/*``) names nothing and is excluded, so a face swept only that way would not enter this population",
  "the sweeps here are generic by construction: one pattern can carry every face under an ancestor, so a module named by an entry point reaches these faces only incidentally -- this face prices reachability of the sweeper, not that the sweep reads any particular face",
  "one hop only: the entry-point class comes from E611's classifier (module basename appearing in an entry file), so a reference composed from a string is a miss",
  "a smoke leg counts as an entry point because it runs whenever the suite runs, and the full suite is not run every round (r1499)",
  "the population is machine-read from E609's published face; a stale E609 face would be graded as published, and population_note says where it came from",
  "modules that touch these faces only through a pattern naming nothing (``*/**/*``) are excluded from the population because they name no ancestor, and are published beside it in no_name_sweeps with their own entry-point class so a dropped non-round script stays visible"
 ],
